{
  "manufacturer": "Carrier",
  "manufacturer_slug": "carrier",
  "model": "Fan Coil Open",
  "model_slug": "fan-coil-open",
  "aliases": [
    "Fan Coil Open",
    "OPN-FC",
    "Carrier Fan Coil controller",
    "11-808-540-01"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Fan coil unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Carrier fan coil units fitted with the Fan Coil Open (OPN-FC) multi-protocol controller.",
  "summary": "The Fan Coil (OPN-FC) controller ships as an integrated part of Carrier packaged fan coil units. DIP switches and the communications selector choose BACnet MS/TP (the default), BACnet ARC156, Modbus or N2, and a LonWorks option card is available. The default device instance is 16101 followed by the two-digit rotary address. Points cover setpoints, space and supply temperatures, fan speed and valve outputs, 2-pipe changeover, alarms and the 'system' points a BAS writes in place of local sensors.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet ARC156"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "16101xx (xx = rotary switch address)",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "System points (system_spt, system_rh, system_iaq, system_oat, system_water_temp, system_stpt_adj) must be written at BACnet priority 16 and no more than once per minute; -999 means no network value.",
    "The guide's generic system-point table also lists system_oaq (AV:1908), oae (BV:1901), press_override (BV:1906) and fire_shutdown (BV:1907). They are not in the Fan Coil points list, so they are left out here.",
    "The points list gives BAS On/Off (keypad_ovrde) as MSV:1, while the system-point table in the same guide shows msv:1001 as on other Open controllers. Check which instance the controller exposes.",
    "Defaults in the points list differ from the sequence text for Fan On Delay (10 s vs 30 s), Fan Off Delay (90 s vs 120 s) and Power Fail Restart Delay (5 s vs 60 s); check on the controller.",
    "Occ Override Delay (AV:9028) is listed twice in the source; it is kept once here. Several display names in the source are just 'Setpoint'; the object name tells you which one.",
    "Each point also has a Modbus register in the same table; only the BACnet side is captured here."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Fan Coil Integration Guide (Appendix A: Fan Coil Network Points List)",
    "doc_number": "11-808-540-01",
    "revision_date": "2022-07-21",
    "url": "https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1000/Public/0E/11-808-540-01.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the Fan Coil Open for BACnet MS/TP with its DIP switches and rotary address. Disable the local Occupancy Schedules so the BAS can command occupancy through keypad_ovrde, then write setpoints directly. Space temperature, humidity, CO2, OAT and 2-pipe water temperature from the BMS go into the system_* points at priority 16 and have to be refreshed within each point's window.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "MV 1",
        "name": "keypad_ovrde",
        "why": "BAS occupancy command: occupied/unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 9001",
        "name": "shutdown",
        "why": "Network shutdown command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 3001",
        "name": "occ_cl_stpt",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 3002",
        "name": "occ_ht_stpt",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 2002",
        "name": "run_status",
        "why": "Current system mode"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 2008",
        "name": "occ_status",
        "why": "Confirms occupied/unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2007",
        "name": "space_temp",
        "why": "Space temperature the unit controls to"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1008",
        "name": "sa_temp",
        "why": "Supply air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 7008",
        "name": "sfan_fail_alarm",
        "why": "Supply fan failure alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 7028",
        "name": "overflow_alarm",
        "why": "Condensate overflow alarm; stops the fan"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "The unit runs occupied 24/7 until a schedule or the BAS takes over. Disable Occupancy Schedules (Configuration > Unit Configuration) so the BAS can control it, then write BAS On/Off keypad_ovrde (MSV:1 in the points list): 1=Inactive, 2=Occupied, 3=Unoccupied. Shutdown (BV:9001) stops the unit from the network. Cool Enable (BV:1011) and Heat Enable (BV:1012) lock out cooling or heating.",
    "heartbeat": "No general heartbeat. Each system point is only used while it is refreshed within its window: space temperature 1 min / 5 min, RH and CO2 5 min / 10 min, OAT and water temperature 5 min / 60 min.",
    "remote_sensors": "Write system_spt (AV:1902), system_rh (AV:1904), system_iaq (AV:1903), system_oat (AV:1901), system_water_temp (AV:1905) and system_stpt_adj (AV:1913) at BACnet priority 16, no more than once a minute. A network value overrides the local sensor while it is refreshed in time. system_water_temp sets the 2-pipe changeover mode and takes priority over the local changeover sensor. The controller clears a system point after processing it, so read the matching control point instead (space_temp, space_rh, iaq, oa_temp, chgovr_mode) at least 30 s after the write.",
    "setup": [
      "MS/TP MAC address is set on the rotary switches (tens and ones); valid 1-99. The address is read only at power-up.",
      "Default device instance is 16101xx (xx = rotary address); it can be changed with an Equipment Touch.",
      "Baud is set on DIP 1-2 (9600/19.2k/38.4k/76.8k); 76.8k is the default; 8N1 fixed. DIP 3 and 4 both Off = BACnet MS/TP.",
      "Set the communications selector to EIA-485; switch changes only take effect after a power cycle.",
      "Max Masters defaults to 127 and Max Info Frames to 10 (adjustable via Equipment Touch). The controller counts as a full load on the MS/TP bus."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "System points must be written at priority 16; writes at any other priority are ignored.",
      "Never write a system point more than once per minute (60 s).",
      "Only controllers set as MS/TP masters answer Who-Is.",
      "The guide says the unit accepts three network demand-limit levels, but cool_demand_level (AV:9006) and heat_demand_level (AV:9036) are listed read-only.",
      "Some points only apply with certain options (2-pipe changeover, electric heat, DCV damper, reheat, humidity sensor, linkage)."
    ]
  },
